      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "c1-l001",
          "runs": [
            {
              "typeface": "roman",
              "text": "Feicǒ. Cuchiuo tozzuru."
            },
            {
              "typeface": "italic",
              "text": " Fechara boca."
            }
          ],
          "note": "Heikou is closing the mouth, kuchi wo tozuru. The particle is uo without a long-o mark; the neighboring tall type had confused OCR."
        },
        {
          "id": "c1-l002",
          "indent": 1,
          "runs": [
            {
              "typeface": "italic",
              "text": "¶ Item. Per met. Ficar vencido, ou con-"
            }
          ],
          "note": "Per met. introduces the figurative sense: being defeated or silenced. Item is the editorial word, not lowercase ltem."
        },
        {
          "id": "c1-l003",
          "indent": 1,
          "runs": [
            {
              "typeface": "italic",
              "text": "cluido na diſputa."
            }
          ],
          "note": "Concluido na disputa completes the figurative explanation: being overcome in a dispute rather than merely shutting the physical mouth."
        },
        {
          "id": "c1-l004",
          "runs": [
            {
              "typeface": "roman",
              "text": "Feifacu. i, Fei."
            },
            {
              "typeface": "italic",
              "text": " Hũs papeis retalhados q̃ſer-"
            }
          ],
          "note": "Heihaku, also hei, refers to cut-paper ritual offerings. The Portuguese papeis retalhados connects it with the preceding page's ritual-wand entry."
        },
        {
          "id": "c1-l005",
          "indent": 1,
          "runs": [
            {
              "typeface": "italic",
              "text": "uem em hũa certa ceremonia diante do Cami."
            }
          ],
          "note": "The paper serves in a ceremony before the kami. Cami is Japanese embedded within the Portuguese sentence, not a Portuguese noun."
        },
        {
          "id": "c1-l006",
          "runs": [
            {
              "typeface": "roman",
              "text": "Feifeito."
            },
            {
              "typeface": "italic",
              "text": " Modo de eſtar a couſa praina. ¶"
            },
            {
              "typeface": "roman",
              "text": " Fei-"
            }
          ],
          "note": "Heiheito describes flatness or calmness. The sea example begins with a divided repetition of that expression."
        },
        {
          "id": "c1-l007",
          "indent": 1,
          "runs": [
            {
              "typeface": "roman",
              "text": "feito xita vmi."
            },
            {
              "typeface": "italic",
              "text": " Mar praino, & quieto. Vt,"
            }
          ],
          "note": "Heiheito shita umi is a smooth, quiet sea, directly matched by mar praino e quieto."
        },
        {
          "id": "c1-l008",
          "indent": 1,
          "runs": [
            {
              "typeface": "roman",
              "text": "Feifeito xitaruno nacani ginuo fari, &c."
            }
          ],
          "note": "Heifeito xitaruno nacani ginuo fari describes pitching a camp on level ground. The second scan pass restores the printed xitaruno, rather than shortening it to xita no, and reads ginuo with gi for ji; both are legitimate Japanese spellings here."
        },
        {
          "id": "c1-l009",
          "indent": 1,
          "runs": [
            {
              "typeface": "roman",
              "text": "Taif"
            },
            {
              "typeface": "italic",
              "text": ". Lib. 30. Aſſentando o arrayal ẽ"
            }
          ],
          "note": "Taif. is the Japanese source label, followed by Portuguese Lib. 30. Assentando o arrayal begins the translation of pitching camp."
        },
        {
          "id": "c1-l010",
          "indent": 1,
          "runs": [
            {
              "typeface": "italic",
              "text": "hum campo largo, & raſo."
            }
          ],
          "note": "Hum campo largo e raso supplies the broad, level field in which the camp is established."
        },
        {
          "id": "c1-l011",
          "runs": [
            {
              "typeface": "roman",
              "text": "Feifǒ."
            },
            {
              "typeface": "italic",
              "text": " Arte de eſgrima. ¶"
            },
            {
              "typeface": "roman",
              "text": " Feifǒuo tçu-"
            }
          ],
          "note": "Heihou means fencing or martial technique here. The example repeats Feifou, not OCR Feitou; the scan supports f in both places."
        },
        {
          "id": "c1-l012",
          "indent": 1,
          "runs": [
            {
              "typeface": "roman",
              "text": "cǒ."
            },
